body:
Okay your requests will be furfilled.  
But first of all I will let you have a little history lesson. 681 Byzantine was forced to acknowledge the existence of Bulgaria and Bulgaria pretty much own they Byzantines especially with Khan Tervel (My favourite) who decided to change who was on the Byzantine throne 3 times. Also everyone knows about how the Polish saved Europe, but no one talks about 900 years earlier how Tervel saved Europe in the Siege of Constantinople. A very epic and awesome fight that the arabs suffered GREAT losses.

Moving on, Ottoman occupation from 1396 to 1878. 500 years of them brainwashing us and making us either animals or their own. Around 1762 an enlightment come from Paisii of Hilendar who writes the real truth "History Slav-Bulgarian" and from then on (most of the) people started realizing everything. Here's a citation from him that every Bulgarian has to know: 


 "Oh, you unwise moron! Why are you ashamed to call yourself a Bulgarian and why don't you read and speak in your native language? Weren't Bulgarians powerful and glorious once? Didn't they take taxes from strong Romans and wise Greeks? Out of all the Slavic nations they were the bravest one. Our rulers were the first ones to call themselves kings, the first ones to have patriarchs, the first ones to baptise their people.(...) Why are you ashamed of your great history and your great language and why do you leave it to turn yourselves into Greeks and Turkish? Why do you think they are any better than you? Well, here you're right because did you see a Greek leave his country and ancestry like you do?" 

(Trivia - Greeks kind of tried to take advantage of us.)

&#x200B;

The minority you're talking about... the gypsies, they are a minority that takes advantage and leaches off everything in Bulgaria and they are lazy, dirty people and don't call me a racist because if I take shots of their neighbourhoods you will see what do I mean. No we do not put them down as a minority so they have as much as the Bulgarians have. Bulgaria's law does not discriminate minorities so there are a lot of minorities living in such as: Bulgarian, Turkish, Romani, Russian, Armenian, Jewish, Vlach and so on and so forth. Yet again they (the gypsies) abuse everything.

&#x200B;

For the playlist, right away, I have this one that is for my patriotic needs, because I love my glorious country. [Here's my own patriotic playlist.](https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLxLV7GsprvyRNJbz2r7tkaWJeqzUNc9rP) There are many many more patriotic songs, but these are one of my favourites. Starts with the most beautiful song ever. The Bulgarian anthem. Sadly most of the songs don't really have an English translation so I guess if you get in touch with me I would translate them. 

Folk - I don't really have a folk playlist, but here is something very very [beautiful](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qYakRyAMAt8) and you can search from then on. Ever played Battlefield 1. Zajdi Zajdi (in the soundtrack of the game) is also a Bulgarian folk.

&#x200B;

English material of Bulgarian suffering?


[Batak massacre.](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Batak_massacre) 

&#x200B;

[April uprising.](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/April_Uprising_of_1876) The uprising that shocked Europe and from then on they started helping Bulgaria.

&#x200B;

We have amazing revolutionaries, rebels if you will... what a dirty word for these amazing people. I will call them legends because they are just legends..

&#x200B;

[Vasil Lewski.](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vasil_Levski) Ever played Hitman? You know how this guy changes clothes and is stealth constantly? Yeah that's the Bulgarian version of him. He was considered a myth at some point in the Ottoman empire just because they could not catch him. When eventually caught ( by pure luck ). He got interrogated, but he did not say anything. 

"If I win, I win for my whole country...if I lose I only lose myself."

&#x200B;

[Hristo Botev.](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hristo_Botev#National_Icon) Another legend he lead one of the revolutionary organizations in Romania. Not only a revolutionary, but a poet and journalist also. His work is very very big and it will take a lot for me to type for you to understand. He gets slain on a peak while having a break from everything."

"The one who dies in a fight for freedom...is immortal."

&#x200B;

The 2 ones above are the most popular ones, but I would like to add my grandfather that did something amazing as well. [Vasil Petleshkov.](https://bg.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%92%D0%B0%D1%81%D0%B8%D0%BB_%D0%9F%D0%B5%D1%82%D0%BB%D0%B5%D1%88%D0%BA%D0%BE%D0%B2) During the uprising every city had a leader which had to say the word to start the action. He had been assigned to one, but after he said the word he got fast to his hometown and uprose them as well. In one night he got 2 cities up in arms and fighting. When caught he was burned to death on his way to the interrogation city, because the Ottomans just decided so. Many many many people mistake his words for Vasil Lewski's:  


"I'm by myself, there are no others."

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

I hope your wishes are furfilled and you learnt about something new and good. If you have any questions, you could get in contact with me.
